// The wall-clock time of day, which is what a "business hours only" rule is written against.
//
// `context.system.now.toTime()` is not determined by the trace: it is a value the request carries
// and the policy reads. So it is modelled as a request field, and its domain -- like every field's
// -- is the values the policy names plus ones on either side, which is what makes both "inside the
// window" and "outside" reachable.
//
// Cedar counts a duration in MILLISECONDS, and so does the model: `duration("9h")` is 32400000.
//
// The discriminating fixture is `business_hours_impossible.dw` beside this one. If the clock were
// admitted but not EVALUATED, this file would be live and so would that one -- and the pair is
// the only thing that tells the two apart.
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"issue_refund",
    resource
)
when {
    context.system.now.toTime() >= duration("9h")
    && context.system.now.toTime() <= duration("17h")
};
